        "severity": "WARNING",
        "location": "longterm-mem/internal/promote/update.go:147-154",
        "claim": "entryFor no longer records PromotedRevision (previously read from the rendered frontmatter). Entries written by promotion/update now always have PromotedRevision 0, so a later hand edit on a page whose entry was written by this code is treated as 'no revision recorded' (wedged) rather than a local edit with a positive revision, changing which refusal path (ErrLocalEditPreserved vs wedge/adopt) applies. isOwnUnrecordedUpdate-style evidence is lost. The comment claims promotion paths 'never did' record it for memorycard pages, but the base recorded it for any page whose frontmatter carried a revision key.",
        "evidence_class": "inferential",
        "causal_disposition": "introduced",
        "proof_refs": [
          "longterm-mem/internal/promote/update.go:147-154"
        ]
      },
